.TH ACPI 8
.SH NAME
acpi \- Advanced Configuration and Power Interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I (in plan9.ini)
.B *acpi=
.PP
.B aux/acpi
[
.B -H
]
[
.B -m
.I mountpoint
]
[
.B -s
.I service
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Aux/acpi
presents at
.I mountpoint
(default
.BR /dev )
an interface to the ACPI. If a
.I service
is specified, the interface will be
posted at
.BI /srv/ service 
as well.
.PP
With the
.B -H
option,
.I aux/acpi
will turn off the power immediately.
.PP
The directory contains the following files.
.TP
.B battery
Contains one line for each battery in the system.  Each line lists 14
fields: the percent charge remaining, power unit used (mW or mA),
remaining capacity, last full charge capacity, design capacity,
warning and low capacity values,
.BR "mV"
separator, present voltage, design voltage, approximate time of charge
left as
.BR hh:mm:ss ,
the status (a string, one of
.BR unknown ,
.BR critical ,
.BR discharging
or
.BR charging ) 
and the charge start and stop limits in percent.
.TP
.B cputemp
Each line provides a current temperature reading of a specific CPU.
.TP
.B pmctl
Writing
.I power off
to
.B pmctl
will turn off the power.
Writing 
.I charge bat min max
to
.B pmctl
will set the upper and lower limit for charging a battery. bat is either
.B "all"
for all batteries or starts with 0.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/aux/acpi.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR reform (1)
.SH BUGS
ACPI itself.
.PP
There are too many ways for controlling battery charging. For now it only works on Thinkpads.
.SH HISTORY
.I Acpi
first appeared in 9front (October, 2016).
